    {
      "id": "insight:6745f6b01936982b",
      "properties": {
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "grounded": true,
        "insight_type": "claim",
        "position_hint": 0.2,
        "routing_tag": "surface",
        "salience": 0.7667,
        "text": "Here's the proposition: for an ordinary investor, is diversification the answer \u2014 or a way to hide from decisions you should be making? Daniel, you first.",
        "tier": 2
      },
      "type": "Insight"
    },
    {
      "id": "insight:bcfb53c35d7b6917",
      "properties": {
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "grounded": true,
        "insight_type": "observation",
        "position_hint": 0.35,
        "routing_tag": "surface",
        "salience": 0.7667,
        "text": "For an individual investor, diversification is the closest thing to a free lunch that exists. You give up almost nothing, and you remove the single biggest way people ruin themselves \u2014 one position\u2026",
        "tier": 2
      },
      "type": "Insight"
    },
    {
      "id": "insight:4db6ad82bb47e6fe",
      "properties": {
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "grounded": true,
        "insight_type": "recommendation",
        "position_hint": 0.5,
        "routing_tag": "surface",
        "salience": 0.7667,
        "text": "And I want to be precise: risk management for individuals is mostly behavioral. The math is easy. Sitting still while a holding gets cut in half is the hard part \u2014 and diversification is what makes\u2026",
        "tier": 2
      },
      "type": "Insight"
    },
    {
      "id": "person:nora",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Nora"
      },
      "type": "Person"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:97fa0c0b4f7b3d1f",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 675,
        "char_start": 521,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "Here's the proposition: for an ordinary investor, is diversification the answer \u2014 or a way to hide from decisions you should be making? Daniel, you first.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 30000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 24000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "person:daniel-cho",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Daniel Cho"
      },
      "type": "Person"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:0cc10f8da8c6b4af",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 927,
        "char_start": 688,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "For an individual investor, diversification is the closest thing to a free lunch that exists. You give up almost nothing, and you remove the single biggest way people ruin themselves \u2014 one position going to zero at the worst possible time.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 36000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 30000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:f383811760efe5cb",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 1139,
        "char_start": 927,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "And I want to be precise: risk management for individuals is mostly behavioral. The math is easy. Sitting still while a holding gets cut in half is the hard part \u2014 and diversification is what makes it survivable.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 42000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 36000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "person:scott-bessent",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Scott Bessent"
      },
      "type": "Person"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:98a5069f94a381be",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 1379,
        "char_start": 1155,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-03",
        "text": "This is where I get off the bus. Concentration with deep understanding beats diversification. Spread across a hundred names and you own things you can't actually judge. That isn't safety \u2014 it's ignorance, evenly distributed.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 48000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 42000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:279eded5e5d8ebbd",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 1659,
        "char_start": 1379,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-03",
        "text": "The way I see it, a portfolio is a system of correlated bets. A handful you understand deeply is more robust than a hundred you don't, because you can see how they move together. Diversifying without understanding just hides the correlation until it's the only thing that matters.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 54000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 48000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:9517f0e0cac4d376",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 1827,
        "char_start": 1666,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "Let me sharpen it, because the disagreement is real. Daniel, Scott says your safety is an illusion. Scott, Daniel says your edge won't survive your own behavior.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 60000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 54000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "insight:authored-p05_e04-0",
      "properties": {
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "grounded": true,
        "insight_type": "claim",
        "position_hint": 0.5,
        "routing_tag": "surface",
        "salience": 1.0,
        "text": "For an individual investor, diversification is the closest thing to a free lunch that exists.",
        "tier": 3
      },
      "type": "Insight"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:authored-p05_e04-0",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 781,
        "char_start": 688,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:daniel-cho",
        "text": "For an individual investor, diversification is the closest thing to a free lunch that exists.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 36000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 30000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "insight:authored-p05_e04-1",
      "properties": {
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "grounded": true,
        "insight_type": "claim",
        "position_hint": 0.5,
        "routing_tag": "surface",
        "salience": 1.0,
        "text": "A portfolio is a system of correlated bets; a handful you understand deeply is more robust than a hundred you don't.",
        "tier": 3
      },
      "type": "Insight"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:authored-p05_e04-1",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 116,
        "char_start": 0,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:scott-bessent",
        "text": "A portfolio is a system of correlated bets; a handful you understand deeply is more robust than a hundred you don't.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 54000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 48000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "insight:authored-p05_e04-2",
      "properties": {
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "grounded": true,
        "insight_type": "claim",
        "position_hint": 0.5,
        "routing_tag": "surface",
        "salience": 1.0,
        "text": "Diversification is the only real risk control \u2014 concentration is how retail investors blow themselves up.",
        "tier": 3
      },
      "type": "Insight"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:authored-p05_e04-2",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 1970,
        "char_start": 1865,
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "speaker_id": "person:daniel-cho",
        "text": "Diversification is the only real risk control \u2014 concentration is how retail investors blow themselves up.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 66000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 60000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p05_e04.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "insight:authored-p05_e04-3",
      "properties": {
        "episode_id": "ep-16ff698c1bd21087",
        "grounded": true,
        "insight_type": "claim",
        "position_hint": 0.5,
        "routing_tag": "surface",
        "salience": 1.0,
        "text": "Concentration with deep understanding beats diversification \u2014 spreading thin is itself the risk, because you end up owning things you can't actually judge.",
        "tier": 3
      },
      "type": "Insight"
    },
